Patchsu patch 500 (optional, pick 0500 and/or 0501): gameplay mods from Ritsu (apply after 0002).

Ported from Ritsu (preritsu/patches/client-offline.patch). Names and acronyms are kept as in Ritsu;
none of them collide with stock osu!lazer mods or with 0501 (Torii). All are osu!standard only.

  Difficulty reduction: Streamline (HST)
  Difficulty increase:  Miss Challenge (MC), No Sliding (NL), One Eye (OE), Decoy Circles (DY), Reversed Sliders (RS)
  Conversion:           Circle Generation (CG), RandomV2 (V2), Spacing Adjust (SA) / Spacing Overtime (SP)
  Fun:                  Metronome (ME)
  System:               Phrase Mirror (PMR), Echo (ECH), Swing (SWG)

Mod select shows a "from Modosu" or "from Ritsu" plaque on each of these mods.

Patchsu additions on top of Ritsu:
- Decoy Circles: "Decoy marking" (cross or combo number), "Decoy number" (0-9), and "Match active combo number"
  (the decoy shows the number the real circle has at that moment in the current combo).
- No Sliding: "Stop converting past threshold (ms)" (shown when converting All sliders): longer sliders are not
  converted; the last tick is "No threshold" (default).
- Scores saved with an unresolved mod (acronym "XX??", e.g. imported before these mods existed or by another client
  sharing the data folder) now resolve to the real mod, and unresolved mods are no longer saved as "XX??".

Replay mod toggles (formerly the separate patch 0007b, old numbering; built only when 0005 is applied too, which defines PATCHSU_REPLAY_MOD_TOGGLES
in Directory.Build.props). These mods join the "Mod effects" group and the clickable mod icons in a replay:
  One Eye        hit objects appear with the beatmap's real approach rate again (only the approach timing
                 changes; positions, stacking and judgements stay exactly as recorded)
  Decoy Circles  decoys become invisible but stay in play, so a click on one still counts as the miss it was
                 (the miss marker still shows where it happened)
  Metronome      the ticks stop
As with 0005, the replay, its score and the results screen are unchanged.

Supporting changes: beatmap-variant plumbing (IBeatmapVariant, converter can detach native objects so variants
never modify the shared beatmap), difficulty mods applied in a defined order (One Eye applies last), the Decoy
Circle hit object (excluded from difficulty, autoplay and hit blocking), hidden mod settings, Ritsu mod icons and
logo embedded in osu.Game. Miss Challenge "Use best local score" reads the active Patchsu profile's scores.

Not ported: Directional Flicks (work in progress in Ritsu itself), Ritsu's replay-player panels for RandomV2 /
Spacing Adjust, RandomV2's "Edit mod live in game" button, Ritsu's Autopilot linearisation tweak.

Modosu-derived files are GPL-3.0 (Modosu by Azuuryy, MOsu by p-720); see LICENCE-Modosu.txt.

